.B tk update
edits the fields supplied on the command line. Omitted fields keep their
Repository Store values.
.PP
Title input trims only outer ASCII spaces and tabs. Body input treats a
leading @ as literal text. The two body sources are mutually exclusive.
.PP
Body input preserves whitespace and line endings. An empty body, file, or
input stream clears the body. NUL is rejected in both title and body.
.PP
Title and body edits can be combined with
.BR \-\-priority ,
.BR \-\-no\-priority ,
.BR \-\-effort ,
.BR \-\-no\-effort ,
.BR \-\-parent ,
or
.BR \-\-no\-parent
for Tickets, in any Selection State.
.B \-\-no\-priority
clears Priority without changing Selection State.
.B \-\-no\-effort
clears Effort.
.PP
The Repository Store commits the edits and queues their Mutations together.
A title-only edit leaves the Backend body alone. A body-only edit leaves the
Backend title alone. Sync sends a supplied title or body even when it matches
the Store. Priority, Effort, and relationship edits sync separately. Effort syncs
on GitHub and stays local on Jira.
